# Index of the type-shape ontology catalog for wasm4pm-compat.
#
# Rule (established this session, recorded in
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-ontology-first-restart-design.md):
# reuse a real, published, dereferenceable public RDF/OWL ontology wherever
# one exists; author one at genuine standards-submission quality only where
# none does, grounded in a real working reference implementation rather
# than invented from field names alone.
#
# Resolved so far (deep-research pass wf_4abe2be2-569, 100 adversarially-
# verified sub-agents):
#   bpmn.ttl  -- reuses sBPMN (Krause et al., ACM K-CAP 2025)
#   log.ttl   -- reuses OCEDO (Latif et al., arXiv:2511.03351)
#   ocel.ttl  -- reuses OCEDO (same ontology, object-centric side)
#   powl.ttl  -- authored fresh (no public POWL ontology exists), grounded
#                in ~/POWL/powl/objects/, at the same header/documentation
#                quality bar OCEDO itself uses
#
# Deferred to a follow-up pass (each needs its own targeted check before
# deciding reuse-vs-author, not assumed from one broad sweep):
# process_tree, petri_net, transition_system, oc_causal_net, ocpn, dfg,
# heuristics_net, org, trie, genetic_matrix, random_variables.

@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

<https://wasm4pm-compat.rs/type-shapes> a owl:Ontology ;
    owl:imports
        <https://sBPMN.github.io/2.0/> ,
        <https://w3id.org/ocedo/core> ,
        <https://w3id.org/ocedo/auxiliary> ,
        <https://w3id.org/powl/core> .
